{
  "notes": "Ambient, A mixolydian, 72 BPM, everything in triplets. A glass pad of slow FM bells (DIGITAL, a soft index, the modulator held), crystal plucks (TRIO, three triangles an octave and two octaves apart) that float in eighth-note triplets through each chord into an 8T echo, the player's glass harmonica on the Smart Keys (a triangle voice, major pentatonic from A3: over the mixolydian VII the C# is a lydian colour, never a clash), and ticks of a minimal kit that fall three against four. No bass and no kick: nothing pulls down. Scenes: A sus2 and the flat VII, two bars each; B leans: each chord lands, then a suspension two beats before the next (6 + 2); C climbs a bar a chord, vi7, VIIadd9, Isus2, IVmaj7 (roots F#, G, A, D); D sinks back through IVmaj7 to the open sus2, two bars each, the glass alone until ENERGY rises. All material is original.",
